@title  PCSA00002 - reach a live game, SWING, and play the ball out
@game   PCSA00002
@shot-every 200

# WHAT THIS RECIPE IS FOR, AND WHY IT IS NOT `into-a-game.recipe`
# --------------------------------------------------------------
# `into-a-game.recipe` arrives at a live game and stops there: a wide shot of the field
# with the batter up, every frame of it a STILL at-bat. Every render question this title
# has been asked was asked at that frame, and it is the reason two faults the user sees in
# seconds have never appeared in a run here - both of them happen when the BALL IS HIT:
# the shape that flashes over the field after contact, and the play that follows it.
#
# A recipe that never swings cannot reach either. This one swings.
#
# HOW THE SWING WORKS, because the timing is not ours to know
# ----------------------------------------------------------
# The CPU pitches on its own schedule and a swing connects only inside a few frames of the
# pitch arriving. Nothing in the emulator can see the pitch, so the recipe does not try to
# time one: it takes a swing on the R TRIGGER (the user's own swing button on this title -
# square never connected in any replay) on a steady cadence across a long window, so
# the swings walk through every phase of the pitcher's cycle rather than landing on one.
# Missing is free - a strike, another pitch - and contact only has to happen once.
#
# `cross` is deliberately NOT the swing here even though it is a swing in this title: it
# is also the button that dismisses every dialog, so a run that presses it during a
# between-innings prompt advances the menu instead, and a recipe cannot tell those apart.

